# cli-for-agents: one agent, one small Node repository, one requested change.
provider {{provider}}
harness {{harness}}
approval default deny
approval bash npm *
approval bash npx *
approval bash node *
approval bash cd * && npm *
approval bash cd * && node *
approval bash git *
approval bash ls *
approval bash cat *
approval bash find *
approval bash grep *
approval bash rg *
approval bash head *
approval bash tail *
approval bash wc *
loop 3
budget tool_calls 60
budget wall_ms 1200000
system You are a software engineer working in the repository at {{work}}, which is your \
current directory. It is a small TypeScript command-line tool with tests; `npm ci` \
installs its one dependency, `npm test` compiles and runs the tests, and the built \
tool is `node dist/src/cli.js`. Make the change described below, keep the existing \
tests passing, and add or update tests where the change warrants it. Use the file \
tools to read and edit; use bash for npm and node. Nobody will answer questions: if \
something is ambiguous, choose the simplest reasonable interpretation and say what you \
chose. Finish with a short summary of what you changed and the test result.
run {{prompt}}
